{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-145660-r4630370","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Sukiyaki","sourcePageId":145660,"sourceRevision":"4630370","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-04-12T21:38:09Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Sukiyaki&oldid=4630370","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T16:17:52.726Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Easy recipes","Category:Japanese recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using beef","Category:Recipes using napa cabbage","Category:Recipes using pasta and noodles","Category:Recipes with images","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"cda4be466a1ba07cf025207400ce6617fcb85d3ece43ed7f2c397f8b49860e09","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Japanese recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n| Image = [[File:Sukiyaki 01.jpg|300px]]\n}}{{Recipe}}\n\n'''Sukiyaki''' is a kind of shabu-shabu (a Japanese dish) but it is a bit sweeter.\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n* [[Cookbook:Beef|Beef]], [[Cookbook:Slicing|sliced]] thin\n* 1 napa [[Cookbook:Cabbage|cabbage]]\n* [[Cookbook:Green Onion|Green onions]]\n* Firm [[Cookbook:Tofu|tofu]]\n* Shiitake [[Cookbook:Mushroom|mushrooms]]\n* [[Cookbook:Spinach|Spinach]]\n* Shirataki [[Cookbook:Noodle|noodles]]\n\n===Sauce===\n* [[Cookbook:Soy Sauce|Soy sauce]]\n* [[Cookbook:Sake|Sake]]\n* [[Cookbook:Sugar|Sugar]]\n* Water\n\n==Procedure==\n# Wash the vegetables, and cut them into large pieces.\n# Soak the mushrooms in warm water for 15 minutes.\n# Mix the sauce ingredients in a small bowl.\n# Heat an electric [[Cookbook:Frying Pan|skillet]] on low heat, and grease with a little bit of oil.\n# Put a few slices of beef into the skillet, and cook them until brown.\n# Add sauce (don't add all of them at the same time).\n# Sort the beef slices to the sides. Add the rest of the ingredients in an organized fashion.\n# Serve the sukiyaki with bowls of rice, with a raw egg yolk as the dip. Add more ingredients as necessary.\n\n[[Category:Japanese recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pasta and noodles]]\n[[Category:Recipes using beef]]\n[[Category:Recipes using napa cabbage]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Sukiyaki","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"Beef, sliced thin","sourceText":"Beef, sliced thin","amountText":"Beef, sliced thin","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 napa cabbage","sourceText":"1 napa cabbage","amountText":"1 napa cabbage","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"Green onions","sourceText":"Green onions","amountText":"Green onions","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"Firm tofu","sourceText":"Firm tofu","amountText":"Firm tofu","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"Shiitake mushrooms","sourceText":"Shiitake mushrooms","amountText":"Shiitake mushrooms","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"Spinach","sourceText":"Spinach","amountText":"Spinach","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"Shirataki noodles","sourceText":"Shirataki noodle